{"nodes": [{"id": "skill_defining_users", "label": "Skill: defining-users (section 9, tasks 9.1-9.2)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "frontmatter + full body", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Roles feed permission requirements and page restrictions; external services feed setup and the integration task."}, {"id": "skill_task_9_1_roles", "label": "Task 9.1 - user roles and their needs", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "skill_task_9_2_stakeholders", "label": "Task 9.2 - other stakeholders: external services, affected parties, the system itself", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "skill_default_single_user_entity_with_role", "label": "Default technical decision: one User entity + a role field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 1 representation", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Simplest for bootcamp products and lets one person hold more than one role; separate entities only when the stored data differs fundamentally, and then say why. Never discuss tables or keys with the trainee - defer to section 13."}, {"id": "skill_question_role_overlap", "label": "Mandatory question: can one person hold two roles, and what must he never do to himself", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 1 overlap warning", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In the real build this was never asked, so a service provider could book his own appointments; it surfaced only during building and then needed blocking in both the UI and the server. The answer becomes a permission rule at task 14.3."}, {"id": "skill_concept_needs_not_features", "label": "Rule: rewrite a need stated as a feature back into a need", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 1 needs", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A need survives a design change; a feature does not."}, {"id": "skill_rule_probe_external_service_mechanics", "label": "Rule: for every external service ask how it will actually work, not just its name", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 2 warning", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "In the real build one question about the meeting mechanism (must the host admit every joiner manually?) changed the product structure: each provider now connects his own account and hosts his own meetings. Ask who owns the account, what the user actually sees, and whether the connection is per-user or one for the whole product; record what each service does, who connects it and what it needs."}, {"id": "skill_concept_system_as_actor", "label": "Concept: the system itself is an actor when things happen with nobody pressing a button", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "project-package/.claude/skills/defining-users/SKILL.md", "source_location": "section 2", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Needed later as a lane in the user-journey diagram (section 11); forgetting it is a listed common mistake."}], "edges": [{"source": "skill_defining_users", "targ